          "description": "<p>A common species on alkaline habitats (Hils et al. 1993), <em>Sarcobatus vermiculatus</em> was found in greatest abundance along the banks of a seasonally wet stream crossing due northeast of MDRS (Fig. 46). Previously placed within the Chenopodiaceae, <em>Sarcobatus</em> is now recognized as the sole genus within the Sarcobataceae (Behnke 1997; APG III 2009). This species was previously recorded for the nearby San Rafael Swell (Harris 1983).</p><p><g>Supplemental File:</strong> CAN 607490 (S",
